  "notes": "Peers: AMD, AVGO, MRVL (AI accelerator, custom silicon and networking competitors). DCF: WACC 10.5% (CAPM judgment; beta, ERP and risk-free rate are assumptions because the snapshot has no rate or index data), terminal growth 3.0%, revenue growth for years 2-5 of 15/10/7/5%, FCF margins 42/44/44/43/42% grounded in CFO minus capex over revenue (FY2024 44.4%, FY2025 46.6%, FY2026 44.8%, TTM 41.9%, H1 FY2027 39.4%, depressed by the receivables and inventory build). dcf_weight 0.7. Offline check with the code's dcf() and peer_multiples() (approximate; code's compute is authoritative): terminal share of EV about 72%, under 80%. UNRESOLVED, material, route to gen-mapping or the lead: net cash in code = cash 22.443B + short_term_investments 0 (unmapped) - debt 33.366B = -10.9B. It omits marketable debt securities of $34.143B (US government and agency, cash-like) and marketable equity securities of $42.783B, both shown on the 2026-07-26 balance sheet in periodic.txt; no XBRL concept in the snapshot carries them. Our judgment: include debt securities, equity securities optional (with a haircut), exclude non-marketable securities ($51.157B). Effect is about +$1.41 per share (debt securities) to +$3.17 per share (both), using 24,285M diluted shares. Inputs were not adjusted to compensate. For the writer and critics: H1 FY2027 net income includes $23.7B of net gains on equity securities (10-Q cash flow statement), so TTM P/E and EPS overstate operating earnings; FCF here is CFO-based and excludes them."
}

